@startuml hld-05b_trading_devboard_slots
title HLD-05b — Trading and Dev Board, widget by widget (UML **object diagram**)\nEach box is a widget instance in a place of that surface's QMainWindow host (panels are QDockWidgets — HLD §11); the link between two of them means **one factory, two surfaces**.\nColour = owning module: green trading · gold strategy · blue market_data · white support.
skinparam objectAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam wrapWidth 170

package "tradingSurface : TradingSurface" <<shell-owned, 0 business logic>> #LightGray {
  object "enableDisable : ActionGroup" as a1 #LightGreen {
    place = HEADER
  }
  object "websocketPill : StatusTile" as a2 #LightGreen {
    place = STATUS_TILE
  }
  object "priceTicker : StatusTile" as a3 #LightBlue {
    place = STATUS_TILE
  }
  object "symbolPicker : ContextBar" as a4 #LightBlue {
    place = CONTEXT_BAR
  }
  object "chartCard : ChartCard" as a5 #White {
    place = WORKSPACE
    symbols = 1
  }
  object "positionsTable : DataTable" as a6 #LightGreen {
    place = RAIL
    order = 10
  }
  object "openOrders : DataTable" as a7 #LightGreen {
    place = RAIL
    order = 20
  }
  object "sessionCard : Panel" as a8 #LightGreen {
    place = RAIL
    order = 30
  }
  object "equityChart : Panel" as a9 #LightGreen {
    place = RAIL
    order = 40
  }
  object "strategyCard : Panel" as a10 #Gold {
    place = RAIL
    order = 50
  }
  object "lastSignal : Panel" as a11 #Gold {
    place = RAIL
    order = 60
  }
  object "appLog : AppLogPanel" as a12 #White {
    place = CONSOLE
  }
}

package "devBoardSurface : DevBoardSurface" <<shell-owned, {dev.mode}>> #LightGray {
  object "enableDisable : ActionGroup" as b1 #LightGreen {
    place = HEADER
  }
  object "websocketPill : StatusTile" as b2 #LightGreen {
    place = STATUS_TILE
  }
  object "priceTicker : StatusTile" as b3 #LightBlue {
    place = STATUS_TILE
  }
  object "systemControls : ControlBar" as b4 #LightBlue {
    place = HEADER
    contents = "market · symbol · date range · load history · start / stop live"
  }
  object "chartCards : ChartCard [*]" as b5 #White {
    place = WORKSPACE
    symbols = "n"
  }
  object "positionsTable : DataTable" as b6 #LightGreen {
    place = RAIL
    order = 10
  }
  object "openOrders : DataTable" as b7 #LightGreen {
    place = RAIL
    order = 20
  }
  object "sessionCard : Panel" as b8 #LightGreen {
    place = RAIL
    order = 30
  }
  object "equityChart : Panel" as b9 #LightGreen {
    place = RAIL
    order = 40
  }
  object "strategyCard : Panel" as b10 #Gold {
    place = RAIL
    order = 50
  }
  object "lastSignal : Panel" as b11 #Gold {
    place = RAIL
    order = 60
  }
  object "orderDialog : Dialog (F9)" as b12 #LightGreen {
    place = RAIL
    order = 70
    {Dev Board only — ADR D15}
  }
  object "indicatorChecklist : Panel" as b13 #White {
    place = RAIL
    order = 80
  }
  object "exchangeApiTester : Probe" as b14 #LightGreen {
    place = DEV_PROBE
  }
  object "appLog : AppLogPanel" as b15 #White {
    place = CONSOLE
  }
}

a1 .. b1 : same factory
a2 .. b2 : same factory
a3 .. b3 : same factory
a5 .. b5 : same factory
a6 .. b6 : same factory
a7 .. b7 : same factory
a8 .. b8 : same factory
a9 .. b9 : same factory
a10 .. b10 : same factory
a11 .. b11 : same factory

note bottom of b12
  **The mirror rule (§4.6.3 rule 2).** Every linked pair above is one
  `factory` value registered against two `surface_id` values — the widget is
  **not coded twice**: 59 duplicated names become 0. The four unlinked
  instances (`systemControls`, `orderDialog`, `indicatorChecklist`,
  `exchangeApiTester`) are what Dev Board holds and Trading does not; the
  reverse never happens.
end note

note bottom of a12
  Both surfaces carry zero business logic of their own. All behaviour lives
  inside the widgets the modules own, and two widgets on the same rail
  coordinate through events and ports — never through the surface handing one
  a reference to another (§4.6.3 rule 5).
end note
@enduml
